WEBVTT

00:00:40.460 --> 00:00:44.570
It feels like I had a nightmare.

00:00:48.360 --> 00:00:50.260
Every time I wake up like this,

00:00:50.260 --> 00:00:52.980
something bad always happens.

00:00:59.430 --> 00:01:02.130
As long as a certain
Modern-Day mage,

00:01:02.130 --> 00:01:04.170
lacking in common sense,

00:01:04.170 --> 00:01:08.010
doesn't involve her student in a crime or anything,
everything should be fine, but...

00:01:11.260 --> 00:01:13.240
I have a bad feeling about this.

00:02:49.380 --> 00:02:52.990
So tall! Amazing! And new!

00:02:52.990 --> 00:02:55.680
Sorry to make you accompany
me on your day off.

00:02:55.680 --> 00:02:58.070
I don't mind at all.

00:02:58.070 --> 00:03:00.990
I've always wanted to come here.

00:03:01.250 --> 00:03:03.510
You're really helping me out.

00:03:03.510 --> 00:03:07.100
I doubt I'll end up helping at all...

00:03:07.100 --> 00:03:11.210
No, just by being here,
you're helping tons.

00:03:12.780 --> 00:03:14.320
With lots of things!

00:03:15.360 --> 00:03:18.880
You're my student, so you should
be more confident.

00:03:18.880 --> 00:03:20.450
Okay, let's go.

00:03:20.970 --> 00:03:22.660
O-Okay!

00:03:41.170 --> 00:03:42.830
Over here.

00:03:42.830 --> 00:03:44.240
Okay!

00:03:48.480 --> 00:03:49.280
A trap?

00:03:50.470 --> 00:03:52.650
The work we're doing is a trap?

00:03:52.650 --> 00:03:54.080
Probably.

00:03:54.610 --> 00:03:57.300
Someone broke in not
too long ago, right?

00:03:57.880 --> 00:04:01.130
Well, someone taking
my things is an issue,

00:04:01.130 --> 00:04:03.580
but they've all been items
that wouldn't earn

00:04:03.580 --> 00:04:04.990
a normal thief a cent.

00:04:05.990 --> 00:04:07.670
That aside,

00:04:07.670 --> 00:04:10.420
isn't it a bit too suspicious that
a request to exterminate

00:04:10.420 --> 00:04:12.060
some apparitions came
in simultaneously?

00:04:12.060 --> 00:04:16.210
So, I thought I'd prepare
and bring you along.

00:04:17.090 --> 00:04:19.330
That's right. If it comes
down to it,

00:04:19.330 --> 00:04:21.330
your Code will be pretty useful.

00:04:21.330 --> 00:04:22.280
Huh?

00:04:23.920 --> 00:04:26.180
Ah, but

00:04:26.180 --> 00:04:29.240
why did you take the job
if it might be a trap?

00:04:29.240 --> 00:04:31.310
Oh, that's...

00:04:36.030 --> 00:04:38.530
Yay, yay, yay.

00:04:43.520 --> 00:04:44.590
Sis!

00:04:46.360 --> 00:04:47.460
Well,

00:04:47.460 --> 00:04:50.600
you know how a seafood hot pot is sometimes
cooked using a heated rock?

00:04:50.600 --> 00:04:52.250
I was trying to make one,

00:04:52.250 --> 00:04:55.660
and when I put the rock in
the oven, it exploded!

00:04:55.660 --> 00:04:57.680
Soshiro got pretty mad.

00:04:58.140 --> 00:05:00.420
Soshiro-san seems really scary...

00:05:00.420 --> 00:05:01.490
He is, right?

00:05:01.490 --> 00:05:04.040
It's going to cost 3,000,000 yen to fix.

00:05:04.040 --> 00:05:05.630
Even if it's a trap,

00:05:05.630 --> 00:05:08.690
I have to take any job I
can to raise the money.

00:05:13.350 --> 00:05:15.600
Looks like it succeeded,

00:05:16.100 --> 00:05:18.200
Jean-Jacques Guibarthez-san.

00:05:30.080 --> 00:05:31.600
How about you die?

00:05:31.950 --> 00:05:34.350
Transform to swords, my Code.

00:05:36.060 --> 00:05:38.430
Pretty amazing. You surprised me.

00:05:39.800 --> 00:05:41.670
But it's useless.

00:05:41.670 --> 00:05:44.600
No matter how talented
a mage you are,

00:05:44.600 --> 00:05:47.780
you can't construct more
Codes than a CPU.

00:05:47.780 --> 00:05:50.100
So your Code of Swords will
never fully materialize.

00:05:50.100 --> 00:05:50.960
In that case-

00:05:51.220 --> 00:05:53.890
You won't be able to summon
any ghostscripts, either.

00:05:54.440 --> 00:05:57.090
This building is brand-new.

00:05:57.090 --> 00:05:59.140
As long as no Codes are ingrained
in the materials,

00:05:59.140 --> 00:06:01.830
there won't be any ghostscripts.

00:06:01.830 --> 00:06:03.960
I guess you've planned
for everything.

00:06:06.240 --> 00:06:09.060
So what do you want from me?

00:06:09.060 --> 00:06:11.160
Have you heard of the
legendary great mage,

00:06:11.160 --> 00:06:13.820
Digitalis Flammalacia?

00:06:14.210 --> 00:06:16.270
What about the Flame Sorceress?

00:06:16.270 --> 00:06:18.840
I'm going to revive her.

00:06:20.550 --> 00:06:24.420
She recorded all the Codes she
accumulated over her lifetime.

00:06:24.860 --> 00:06:30.530
In order to obtain this Sorceress's
Library, I will revive her.

00:06:32.420 --> 00:06:33.360
I see.

00:06:33.830 --> 00:06:37.350
I can reverse assemble
the library.

00:06:37.850 --> 00:06:43.080
We can change the world and teach all men and
women the wisdom of Classical Magic.

00:06:43.310 --> 00:06:45.050
If you revive the Flame Sorceress,

00:06:45.050 --> 00:06:47.700
a building like this will turn
to little more than dust.

00:06:47.700 --> 00:06:49.500
Are you serious about this?

00:06:49.500 --> 00:06:51.110
Starting a month ago,

00:06:51.110 --> 00:06:53.410
I've been constructing Codes
encompassing the building.

00:06:53.410 --> 00:06:54.840
I can't go back.

00:06:54.840 --> 00:06:55.600
And furthermore...

00:06:56.820 --> 00:06:57.890
Furthermore?

00:06:59.120 --> 00:07:02.900
The girl who will act as the container
for Digitalis is already inside.

00:07:07.020 --> 00:07:09.890
I'm not fake!

00:07:09.890 --> 00:07:13.030
That just upsets me.

00:07:13.410 --> 00:07:16.780
I'm going to show you
exactly what happens

00:07:16.780 --> 00:07:19.410
when you don't take
me seriously, Misa!

00:07:22.200 --> 00:07:23.770
I'm sorry.

00:07:23.770 --> 00:07:26.780
There isn't anything by that
name in this building.

00:07:28.020 --> 00:07:30.920
You don't know anything
about apparitions at

00:07:30.920 --> 00:07:32.500
a WLAN hotspot here?

00:07:33.450 --> 00:07:34.870
Apparitions?

00:07:37.800 --> 00:07:39.210
Just as I thought...

00:07:39.540 --> 00:07:41.300
Um, um... Is it okay for us

00:07:41.300 --> 00:07:43.140
to be here, even though
it's a trap?

00:07:43.140 --> 00:07:44.010
Yeah.

00:07:44.220 --> 00:07:47.070
I have to stay here to figure out

00:07:47.070 --> 00:07:48.930
what traps they've set for me.

00:07:48.930 --> 00:07:51.360
But it's dangerous here!

00:07:51.580 --> 00:07:54.340
If you're being targeted, it's
dangerous everywhere.

00:07:54.740 --> 00:07:58.570
I have to figure out the kind of
traps they're laying for me.

00:07:58.570 --> 00:08:02.170
Well, if they're trying to
use Modern-Day Magic,

00:08:02.170 --> 00:08:05.020
then they actually should
be avoiding me, but...

00:08:05.020 --> 00:08:05.890
Right...

00:08:05.890 --> 00:08:07.500
In any event,

00:08:07.500 --> 00:08:10.490
I'm saving our best
weapon for last,

00:08:10.490 --> 00:08:11.880
so I'm sure it'll work out.

00:08:11.880 --> 00:08:13.400
No, it won't!

00:08:13.680 --> 00:08:14.600
Yumiko-chan!

00:08:13.930 --> 00:08:16.100
Every time you're about
to commit some crime,

00:08:14.600 --> 00:08:16.010
Yumiko?

00:08:16.100 --> 00:08:18.550
you always hide it from me!

00:08:18.550 --> 00:08:21.610
Th-That's not what's happening
today, Yumiko-chan!

00:08:21.890 --> 00:08:24.680
Well, I did think of asking
you to come,

00:08:24.680 --> 00:08:28.250
but then I thought I shouldn't get
you too involved this time...

00:08:28.250 --> 00:08:31.420
And on what, exactly,
do you base that?

00:08:31.630 --> 00:08:32.800
My intuition?

00:08:32.800 --> 00:08:33.600
Intuition?!

00:08:33.870 --> 00:08:38.020
You must be up to
something shady!

00:08:38.020 --> 00:08:40.360
You take care of her.

00:08:43.310 --> 00:08:45.030
Sorry about that!

00:08:45.640 --> 00:08:47.490
Wait up, you criminal!

00:08:47.490 --> 00:08:49.540
I can't breathe!

00:08:47.490 --> 00:08:49.540
Hurry up and get off me, Koyomi!

00:09:01.290 --> 00:09:02.480
Let's see here...

00:09:19.320 --> 00:09:21.880
So it was you.

00:09:23.080 --> 00:09:26.510
It's been a while, Anehara Misa-san.

00:09:26.510 --> 00:09:29.660
You sure went to a lot
of trouble just for me.

00:09:30.130 --> 00:09:34.330
You set a trap on a plane
to distract me

00:09:34.330 --> 00:09:38.660
while you stole Kenjuro's
sword from my home storage.

00:09:39.240 --> 00:09:41.870
And then I called you here.

00:09:41.870 --> 00:09:44.450
Stealing's a crime, you know?

00:09:44.960 --> 00:09:48.660
I never thought I'd hear something
like that from you.

00:09:49.030 --> 00:09:51.940
There's a big difference between a
grey area and something wrong.

00:09:52.320 --> 00:09:54.980
Is that why you'll try to stop me?

00:09:54.980 --> 00:09:59.400
Access to magic should be
universal and unlimited.

00:09:59.400 --> 00:10:03.070
You can't master Codes
unless you get them,

00:10:03.070 --> 00:10:04.360
one by one, yourself.

00:10:04.360 --> 00:10:06.220
With your methods,

00:10:06.220 --> 00:10:08.730
even a hundred years from now,
magic use won't have spread.

00:10:08.730 --> 00:10:10.880
Humans are not that foolish.

00:10:11.300 --> 00:10:13.860
Looks like we simply can't agree.

00:10:13.860 --> 00:10:18.120
What are you planning by summoning
Guibarthez's ghostscript?

00:10:18.370 --> 00:10:22.080
The Sorceress's Library
is my ultimate goal.

00:10:22.080 --> 00:10:24.880
Then, I'll just have to
stop you by force.

00:10:24.880 --> 00:10:26.340
Whoa there.

00:10:26.340 --> 00:10:29.960
It's too risky for you to
stand against me.

00:10:29.960 --> 00:10:32.610
I'd rather have you fight
it out with your allies

00:10:32.610 --> 00:10:34.300
in this building.

00:10:34.300 --> 00:10:35.390
What was that?

00:10:35.700 --> 00:10:37.140
Now, now.

00:10:37.140 --> 00:10:39.920
If you really intend to stop
the Sorceress's Library,

00:10:39.920 --> 00:10:41.690
listen to what I have to say.

00:10:41.920 --> 00:10:43.070
What do you mean?

00:10:58.970 --> 00:11:00.390
What do you think?

00:11:00.960 --> 00:11:02.590
Now you've done it...

00:11:22.250 --> 00:11:26.150
Jeez... Why is Misa
like that, anyway?

00:11:26.430 --> 00:11:29.380
As soon as she starts doing something
shady, she keeps it all a secret.

00:11:29.380 --> 00:11:33.650
How did you know Misa-san
was going to be there?

00:11:34.440 --> 00:11:36.080
I got an e-mail.

00:11:36.080 --> 00:11:37.130
An e-mail?

00:11:37.130 --> 00:11:39.370
But the sender was unknown.

00:11:47.610 --> 00:11:49.210
It said that Anehara Misa

00:11:49.210 --> 00:11:52.150
was planning something
big in this building.

00:11:52.150 --> 00:11:54.310
Something big?

00:11:54.310 --> 00:11:56.820
I thought it was a prank,

00:11:56.820 --> 00:11:59.520
but just to be safe, I
called Misa's house,

00:11:59.520 --> 00:12:02.660
and Soshiro said she's
headed over here.

00:12:03.490 --> 00:12:06.580
Then I knew that something
was going on.

00:12:06.930 --> 00:12:10.620
B-But Misa-san said this
might be a trap.

00:12:10.620 --> 00:12:13.400
A trap? What kind?

00:12:14.840 --> 00:12:16.880
I don't know...

00:12:17.250 --> 00:12:19.340
Then we really need
to pin Misa down.

00:12:22.520 --> 00:12:24.430
What's wrong, Yumiko-chan?

00:12:24.430 --> 00:12:25.850
A human-vanishing Code...

00:12:27.610 --> 00:12:28.890
No one's here!

00:12:28.890 --> 00:12:30.320
It must have been Misa!

00:12:32.750 --> 00:12:33.780
The door, it's...!

00:12:33.780 --> 00:12:34.470
Koyomi!

00:12:37.090 --> 00:12:37.860
Koyomi!

00:12:38.160 --> 00:12:39.850
It's going to close!

00:12:42.480 --> 00:12:44.370
Ow...

00:12:44.370 --> 00:12:45.420
Koyomi!

00:12:46.080 --> 00:12:47.270
Koyomi!

00:12:48.890 --> 00:12:50.450
Yumiko-chan!

00:12:50.450 --> 00:12:51.900
Get away from the door!

00:12:52.540 --> 00:12:54.390
Transform to swords, my Code!

00:12:57.300 --> 00:12:58.610
Not happening.

00:12:59.410 --> 00:13:02.300
It's made to withstand fires
of up to 5,432°F.

00:13:02.300 --> 00:13:04.260
No matter how good you
are, it's not happening.

00:13:04.260 --> 00:13:07.710
Also, I put a Code
in the computer,

00:13:07.710 --> 00:13:10.420
so you won't be able to open
it with Classical Magic.

00:13:11.200 --> 00:13:13.070
What's going on?

00:13:13.500 --> 00:13:15.440
I want to talk, just us.

00:13:16.790 --> 00:13:18.420
You're not done yet?

00:13:18.420 --> 00:13:21.210
Yumiko-chan, you're
not done yet?

00:13:21.210 --> 00:13:23.490
Yumiko-chan!

00:13:35.980 --> 00:13:39.800
To trap your own student in there
just so you can talk to me,

00:13:39.800 --> 00:13:41.660
something must be wrong
in your head.

00:13:41.940 --> 00:13:44.140
Koyomi's fine.

00:13:44.140 --> 00:13:46.020
She's quite capable,

00:13:46.020 --> 00:13:48.450
so she'll be able to get
out on her own.

00:13:48.450 --> 00:13:50.670
That's not the problem here!

00:13:50.670 --> 00:13:52.470
Then why not take me down?

00:13:53.170 --> 00:13:54.680
You'll be able to save Koyomi.

00:13:58.020 --> 00:14:00.880
Anehara Kenjuro's
sword was stolen.

00:14:02.620 --> 00:14:04.500
Jean-Jacques Guibarthez...

00:14:04.930 --> 00:14:07.390
That sword is in this building.

00:14:07.390 --> 00:14:10.530
That's why I don't want you here.

00:14:10.900 --> 00:14:12.960
Will you let me take care of it?

00:14:12.960 --> 00:14:15.410
I'm not who I was six years ago.

00:14:15.790 --> 00:14:18.420
I can handle a little heat!

00:14:20.140 --> 00:14:25.290
If you won't leave, I'll
have to make you.

00:14:25.290 --> 00:14:27.220
I was thinking it was about time

00:14:27.220 --> 00:14:32.210
that we saw exactly which
of us is stronger.

00:14:32.590 --> 00:14:36.070
And I do need to save Koyomi.

00:14:36.070 --> 00:14:37.870
You're pretty confident.

00:14:37.870 --> 00:14:40.400
Indeed. That, I am.

00:14:42.680 --> 00:14:44.740
Transform to swords, my Code!

00:14:46.880 --> 00:14:48.150
It's begun.

00:14:48.150 --> 00:14:50.650
Yes, just as planned.

00:14:51.050 --> 00:14:53.130
If we cancel out Cristbarth's Curse

00:14:53.130 --> 00:14:56.790
at the moment of Anehara
Misa's victory,

00:14:56.790 --> 00:14:59.050
Digitalis will revive.

00:14:59.050 --> 00:15:01.750
It appears that there's another
Code operator.

00:15:02.380 --> 00:15:05.250
If you think she's in the way,
I can get rid of her.

00:15:05.580 --> 00:15:07.770
Otherwise, I'll just
leave her there.

00:15:10.850 --> 00:15:13.080
Yumiko-chan, are you done yet?

00:15:13.490 --> 00:15:16.570
Are you done yet, Yumiko-chan?!

00:15:17.720 --> 00:15:20.260
Huh? Yumiko-chan?

00:15:20.570 --> 00:15:22.830
You mean no one's there?

00:15:22.830 --> 00:15:25.770
Is anyone... Is anyone there?

00:15:25.770 --> 00:15:27.620
Anyone?!

00:15:28.190 --> 00:15:30.460
Wh-What should I do?

00:15:30.460 --> 00:15:32.790
Misa-san and Yumiko-chan
aren't here, either...

00:15:33.090 --> 00:15:35.560
Oh, I-I know!

00:15:35.560 --> 00:15:36.970
Ta-dah!

00:15:36.970 --> 00:15:39.550
If I just call Kaho-chan...

00:15:39.550 --> 00:15:43.080
Let's see, Kaho-chan's
number is...

00:15:43.410 --> 00:15:45.360
Th-There we go.

00:15:47.800 --> 00:15:52.640
The number you have dialed
is currently not in use...

00:15:50.090 --> 00:15:53.520
Wh-Why? That should
have been right.

00:15:54.090 --> 00:15:57.730
Ah! I-I didn't have enough digits?!

00:15:54.830 --> 00:15:59.300
Sakazaki Kaho

00:15:57.730 --> 00:16:00.680
Why?! <i>What should I do?!</i>

00:16:05.270 --> 00:16:07.400
Transform to swords, my Code!

00:16:16.020 --> 00:16:17.580
You're pretty good.

00:16:17.580 --> 00:16:18.870
You, too.

00:16:21.260 --> 00:16:23.050
Transform to swords, my Code.

00:16:27.810 --> 00:16:28.750
I see.

00:16:29.920 --> 00:16:31.570
Transform to swords, my-

00:16:35.090 --> 00:16:36.380
St. Elmo?

00:16:39.540 --> 00:16:40.380
Whoops.

00:16:40.380 --> 00:16:43.110
I grounded myself
to avoid Codes.

00:16:43.110 --> 00:16:46.430
Making my cell phone ring
is something you'd do.

00:16:46.920 --> 00:16:50.920
I told you to set it on vibrate.

00:16:53.040 --> 00:16:55.200
I want to ask you one thing.

00:16:55.770 --> 00:16:57.430
Are you serious about this?

00:17:02.670 --> 00:17:04.570
O-Of course.

00:17:04.570 --> 00:17:06.970
I'm always serious!

00:17:07.440 --> 00:17:09.850
Then no hard feelings,
whoever loses.

00:17:09.850 --> 00:17:11.470
You don't need to tell me that!

00:17:11.940 --> 00:17:14.330
If something happens to me,
have Soshiro help you.

00:17:14.990 --> 00:17:17.680
He's my final weapon.

00:17:17.680 --> 00:17:19.410
What are you talking about?

00:17:19.410 --> 00:17:21.390
Transform to swords, my Code!

00:17:24.170 --> 00:17:25.860
I'm gonna be serious now.

00:17:29.480 --> 00:17:30.770
It's scary!

00:17:30.770 --> 00:17:33.400
At this rate, what do
I do if no one comes?

00:17:35.500 --> 00:17:37.640
If you run into trouble,

00:17:37.640 --> 00:17:40.220
open the battery compartment
on your cell.

00:17:40.220 --> 00:17:42.090
It might help.

00:17:43.760 --> 00:17:45.990
O-Oh yeah, I remember!

00:17:47.330 --> 00:17:49.550
Thank you, Kaho-chan!

00:17:53.590 --> 00:17:54.540
Hello?

00:17:54.780 --> 00:17:56.360
Kaho-chan?

00:17:56.360 --> 00:17:58.470
Thank goodness...

00:17:58.470 --> 00:18:00.370
Um, there was your cell,

00:18:00.370 --> 00:18:04.220
and then a fire door, with
your number wrong.

00:18:04.220 --> 00:18:07.060
And then I felt better
because of what

00:18:07.060 --> 00:18:08.570
you put in the back of my phone.

00:18:08.570 --> 00:18:10.430
And it was useful, so I called you!

00:18:10.810 --> 00:18:14.380
How about you tell me what happened
in order, Morishita?

00:18:15.550 --> 00:18:16.950
I see.

00:18:16.950 --> 00:18:20.200
So Misa-san used a human-vanishing Code,

00:18:20.200 --> 00:18:22.950
and after that, a fire
door came down.

00:18:22.950 --> 00:18:25.130
Yeah, that's it!

00:18:25.660 --> 00:18:28.690
It looks like Yumiko-chan isn't
here anymore, either.

00:18:28.690 --> 00:18:31.480
No one's coming to help me.

00:18:31.800 --> 00:18:34.010
I believe you were trapped
there deliberately.

00:18:34.010 --> 00:18:34.880
Huh?

00:18:35.760 --> 00:18:38.110
Th-That's mean...

00:18:38.110 --> 00:18:42.140
Wh... Wh-Wh-Wh-What should
I do, Kaho-chan?

00:18:42.400 --> 00:18:45.890
I believe that a Code is
running through the

00:18:45.890 --> 00:18:47.930
computer controlling that door.

00:18:48.350 --> 00:18:52.550
So I believe it should open
if you nullify the Code.

00:18:53.590 --> 00:18:56.450
I'll go over all the
possibilities now.

00:18:56.450 --> 00:18:58.810
Basically, all we can do
is try different things.

00:18:58.810 --> 00:19:00.460
G-Got it.

00:19:00.460 --> 00:19:01.880
Hey, Kaho-chan.

00:19:01.880 --> 00:19:02.500
Huh?

00:19:03.020 --> 00:19:04.660
I wonder if they're okay.

00:19:04.660 --> 00:19:05.660
Okay?

00:19:05.660 --> 00:19:10.310
I feel Misa-san and Yumiko-chan's
Codes on the roof right now,

00:19:10.310 --> 00:19:13.230
but it feels like the Codes
are going at each other.

00:19:13.230 --> 00:19:13.760
Huh?

00:19:14.850 --> 00:19:16.760
I hope they're okay.

00:19:19.440 --> 00:19:21.700
Transform to swords, my Code!

00:19:41.630 --> 00:19:45.240
If she gets me with her
next Code, it's all over.

00:19:54.620 --> 00:19:56.800
It's the moment of truth, Yumiko.

00:19:57.170 --> 00:19:58.760
You ready?

00:20:19.890 --> 00:20:21.450
Thanks, Kaho-chan.

00:20:21.450 --> 00:20:23.120
The door opened.

00:20:23.120 --> 00:20:24.400
That's good,

00:20:24.400 --> 00:20:27.340
but I think you should get away
from there as soon as possible.

00:20:27.340 --> 00:20:28.790
Yeah, I got it!

00:20:28.790 --> 00:20:29.280
Huh?

00:20:29.870 --> 00:20:31.140
What is it?

00:20:31.140 --> 00:20:32.790
The sky is shining...

00:20:34.000 --> 00:20:36.340
So everything went as planned?

00:20:36.680 --> 00:20:39.970
I didn't think it would
go so easily.

00:20:39.970 --> 00:20:42.300
So what will you do next?

00:20:43.620 --> 00:20:46.990
I've already thought
of the next phase.

00:20:56.230 --> 00:20:57.360
Rain...

00:22:57.980 --> 00:22:58.610
Misa!

00:22:59.190 --> 00:23:00.160
Misa!

00:23:00.460 --> 00:23:01.360
Misa!

00:23:01.630 --> 00:23:03.730
Misa, answer me!

00:23:04.950 --> 00:23:06.250
Misa!

00:23:07.290 --> 00:23:08.360
Misa!

00:23:08.910 --> 00:23:11.730
1, 2, 3...

00:23:12.500 --> 00:23:14.660
1, 2, 3...

00:23:14.660 --> 00:23:17.050
1, 2, 3...

00:23:17.340 --> 00:23:19.380
1, 2, 3...

00:23:20.060 --> 00:23:22.140
Oh, I know. Then I should...

00:23:38.900 --> 00:23:42.980
<i>Misa!</i>

00:23:46.370 --> 00:23:49.530
The Modern-Day Magic mage who vanished,
leaving behind the smell of death...

00:23:49.530 --> 00:23:52.620
The Classical Magic girl wandering
on a search for her...

00:23:52.620 --> 00:23:55.600
They stage themselves
in the town of destiny.

00:23:55.600 --> 00:23:58.950
The Cyber City, Akihabara...

00:24:04.650 --> 00:24:07.120
Lesson 9. Blu-ray and DVD

00:24:07.540 --> 00:24:14.460
Ebisu, Tokyo JR Station, West Exit

00:24:08.170 --> 00:24:11.660
Hello, Morishita Koyomi here!

00:24:11.660 --> 00:24:13.880
Anehara Misa here!

00:24:13.880 --> 00:24:17.240
What are we going
to study today?

00:24:17.240 --> 00:24:21.520
Today, we're going over
Blu-rays and DVDs.

00:24:21.690 --> 00:24:26.100
Um, another shameless
promotion?

00:24:26.100 --> 00:24:30.010
Hey, there! Let's have
fun promoting!

00:24:30.010 --> 00:24:31.490
Okay!

00:24:31.490 --> 00:24:38.520
<i>Yoku Wakaru Gendai Mahou</i>
vol. 1, goes on sale 10/23.

00:24:38.520 --> 00:24:41.870
Blu-rays and DVDs are
both being released.

00:24:41.870 --> 00:24:45.330
The vol. 1 limited first press edition version
includes a special disc

00:24:45.330 --> 00:24:48.180
containing the unaired episode 0,

00:24:48.180 --> 00:24:50.310
"Cruncha Cruncha Cruncha,"

00:24:50.310 --> 00:24:57.810
as well as the special that
aired prior to the series.

00:24:58.910 --> 00:25:00.500
That's wonderful!

00:25:00.500 --> 00:25:03.410
Also included is a special booklet

00:25:03.410 --> 00:25:11.010
and a CD-ROM for the <i>Yoku Wakaru
Gendai Mahou Web Radio #1</i>.

00:25:11.010 --> 00:25:13.030
Of course, the jacket is drawn

00:25:13.030 --> 00:25:17.110
by the illustrator of the original
works, Miyashita Miki-san!

00:25:17.110 --> 00:25:19.730
That's quite a lot!

00:25:19.730 --> 00:25:21.310
On top of all that,

00:25:21.310 --> 00:25:24.350
textless versions of the
opening and ending,

00:25:24.350 --> 00:25:27.540
as well as an audio commentary,
are included.

00:25:27.540 --> 00:25:30.470
Wow! What a bargain!

00:25:30.820 --> 00:25:34.830
Misa-san, aren't you
slacking off a bit?

00:25:34.830 --> 00:25:37.120
Nope, just your imagination!

00:25:37.120 --> 00:25:40.090
Anyway, it's almost
time, Koyomi.

00:25:40.090 --> 00:25:42.130
I'll let you sum everything up.

00:25:42.130 --> 00:25:43.750
Okay.

00:25:43.750 --> 00:25:52.180
<i>Yoku Wakaru Gendai Mahou</i> Vol. 1
Blu-rays and DVDs go on sale 10/23!

00:25:52.180 --> 00:25:55.480
Okay, did all of you
remember that?

00:25:55.880 --> 00:25:59.420
That's it for class today.

00:25:59.420 --> 00:26:01.310
See you later!

00:26:01.310 --> 00:26:04.930
We're taking pre-orders!

00:26:04.930 --> 00:26:07.990
Bye-bye!
